(7078198, 1076373, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Nice classic car. The color toning and the overlay really give this a feel of looking through a photo album, finding the page, and then recalling fond memories of one''s first car.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Nice classic car. The color toning and the overlay really give this a feel of looking through a photo album, finding the page, and then recalling fond memories of one''s first car.', '2013-07-28 21:14:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(7078199, 1076185, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Love the title of the photo that not only plays with the meaning by giving the photo an aged/retro look but also ''directional'' travel. The escalator shot has the coming and going of people in the two states of travel (up and down). The overlay and faded tones gives this shot the feel of an aged photograph - one that has markings of the passage of time given the fade spots on the bottom right corner and a bit on the left side edge.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Love the title of the photo that not only plays with the meaning by giving the photo an aged/retro look but also ''directional'' travel. The escalator shot has the coming and going of people in the two states of travel (up and down). The overlay and faded tones gives this shot the feel of an aged photograph - one that has markings of the passage of time given the fade spots on the bottom right corner and a bit on the left side edge.', '2013-07-28 21:19:44.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(7078206, 1076247, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Very good lighting and pose that is a nice homage to Russell Lee''s work (you made me curious so I googled and enjoyed spending some time looking at his work). I think I see the texture overlay but it is very subtle on the homesteader and the wood post (I think it is adding some color toning). Where I see it most is in the sky (it looks to be a concrete wall or wall with two shades to it). The only suggestion I would have to improve the shot and conjure up a stronger impression that the gent is a homesteader is to mayhap used a different overlay texture which would have given the skintones a look that he indeed works out in the sun (I''m basing this on the photo of Lee''s Homesteader in the cornfield where he clearly has the skin tones of a man who works out in the sun and bears the marks on his face) Still a great photo but wonder if the overlay might be too subtle for some of the DPC crowd.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Very good lighting and pose that is a nice homage to Russell Lee''s work (you made me curious so I googled and enjoyed spending some time looking at his work). I think I see the texture overlay but it is very subtle on the homesteader and the wood post (I think it is adding some color toning). Where I see it most is in the sky (it looks to be a concrete wall or wall with two shades to it). The only suggestion I would have to improve the shot and conjure up a stronger impression that the gent is a homesteader is to mayhap used a different overlay texture which would have given the skintones a look that he indeed works out in the sun (I''m basing this on the photo of Lee''s Homesteader in the cornfield where he clearly has the skin tones of a man who works out in the sun and bears the marks on his face) Still a great photo but wonder if the overlay might be too subtle for some of the DPC crowd.', '2013-07-28 21:34:58.000000', NULL, 1),
